{"type":"message","id":"f7ebc9a0","parentId":"4b9a55bf","timestamp":"2026-05-17T04:05:03.035Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still 1101. Let me try something completely different - maybe the POST endpoint needs form data instead of JSON. Or maybe I should check if maybe a `target` field is needed.\n\nActually, wait. Let me look at the message more carefully. The messages in the history have `replyTo: null`. What if I need to include a valid replyTo ID instead of null? But that doesn't make sense for a new message.\n\nHmm, or maybe the issue is that the `threadId` needs to be set to just \"arbitration\" or maybe with a different format. Let me check if there's a `target` field.\n\nActually, I wonder if the issue is something else entirely. \n\nI can't inspect the actual API documentation, so let me experiment with different content types like text/plain and application/x-www-form-urlencoded to see if the endpoint is picky about formats, or maybe I should try using a query parameter instead of a header for the API key.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n\n1101 持续。让我尝试表单编码格式（排除 JSON 问题）：\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-da8b615e-6721-4a21-9c60-2631433617e2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try form-encoded instead of JSON\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=test\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a95bf017-6381-47b6-a8d2-e9ff36f8cc93","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try without any body or with different combinations\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","u