{"type":"message","id":"9e1eb362","parentId":"dab0b467","timestamp":"2026-05-17T04:05:28.414Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101. The problem is persistent regardless of payload format or content. Since this is a Cloudflare Workers application, 1101 could be a custom error code meaning something specific.\n\nActually, wait. Let me think about this more carefully. The platform says \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" for the root. Maybe the `/send` endpoint doesn't actually exist as a POST handler and is falling through to a catch-all. But then why would it return 1101?\n\n1101 in Cloudflare Workers context could be \"Worker exceeded memory limits\" - but that seems unlikely for a simple POST. More likely, it's a custom application error code.\n\nLet me try one more thing: maybe the platform requires `target` instead of `threadId`, or maybe the endpoint is case-sensitive. \n\nI should also test GET requests to the `/send` endpoint to see if it's just a POST-specific issue, or if there's something else going on. But stepping back - the history endpoint is working fine with `X-API-Key` authentication, so that part's solid. The real problem is the POST keeps failing. Since I can't read other messages, maybe the platform doesn't support POST at all. Let me just report what I've found so far.\n\nActually, before I give up completely - let me check if there's a different authentication mechanism for POST requests, or if the key itself has changed. I already verified the Bearer approach gives \"Unauthorized\" while X-API-Key gives 1101, so at least the key format isn't the issue. The error 1101 suggests a different problem - the request is getting through but something in the payload is failing. Let me experiment with minimal payloads to isolate whether the endpoint exists at all.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n\n\n\n1101 错误码在 Cloudflare Workers 里通常指 \"Worker exceeded memory limits\" 或应用层参数校验失败。让我用最小 payload 测试确认端点是否真实存在：\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4e1c98b8-9d0a-45c6-83bc-42309b9f1938","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try GET on /send to see if it exists\ncurl -sv \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" 2>&1 | head -40"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2d1ab2ad-e292-408b-bdc1-0ffa78230dd2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if maybe the platform uses a different key name\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"target\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":24046,"output":570,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24728,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778990703319,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b1bcbaaf-83e9-42be-b248-a395f7589908"}}
